<<~ ahu slot=`#/3-rulings-and-laws-taken-this-seat`>>

!! 3. Rulings and laws taken this seat (fold into the road's #/rulings at the true-up)
* Operator 2026-11-07: ''decide forks by talk-out'' under the house laws (No global now · no back-compat in early alpha · causal islands · identity-as-relation · Infrastructure-as-Myth); never park "only the operator can decide". (memory: feedback_lares_talk_out_before_surfacing.md)
* Operator 2026-11-07: ''pentabarf V'' — canon grew fast; test and collide it against code; uncertainty spike → Luna-class two-wave pass, then mu talk-story. (memory: feedback_pentabarf_v_collide_canon.md)
* Controller, talked out: ''the face delegation lease retires''; whole-fleet removal = remove-wins set-asides on KNOWN dyads (census refuses an incomplete view) or the K18 re-anchor once K18 lands. The "kāpae over the face" option DROPPED (canon names four marked edges; Luna collide). 'owing' counts as standing (house standingOfReading).
* Controller: ''a lock always drops its signer'' (security outranks durability; clock-sweep F1).
* Controller: ''"cure-after" on the lane whose job it is reads as build-a-now-b-later'' (Kiaʻi's lean, accepted): cures land inside the lane.
* Controller: the boot wait renews only on monotone ''boot milestones'' (Kiaʻi's lean).
* Controller: l27 route references bind a digest of the operation's identifying arguments where the parking caller knows them.
* Controller: ''the read-back waiver is an explicit harness act'' in the process that reads the card, seated once in the CLI's shared test setup; refusal tests clear it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/4-practices-this-seat-learned`>>

!! 4. Practices this seat learned (worth the crew note)
* ''Read the CI report artifact, not the log.'' Truncated logs sent two triage reads the wrong way on lease-end; the shard's JSON report named face-join in one line.
* ''"Green on the named files" ≠ green on what CI runs.'' Run the whole package locally for non-daemon packages (lares-cli: 44 reds hid behind named-file greens).
* ''Every P1 marked INFER gets a run'' before acceptance or dismissal (l27's F1: inferred one test, the run showed six).
* ''Codex vs Opus at seams'' (testimony, not a ruling): Terra stalled on cross-package custody seams three times (b5b drain, clock-sweep tail, lease-end grants); Opus seam leads cured each in one step; Sol cured l27 item 4 and door-fix in single steps where Terra stalled. Worth the owed tiers measure.
* ''Stricter instruments find real holes'': "never ack silently" exposed the herm's lost boot writes and their browser mirror; the blind door read exposed the shared node_modules inodes.
* A `.mem`-only head over a red parent draws no CI run: dispatch `gh workflow run CI --ref <branch>`.
* Land-train drops a lane on a merge-tree conflict: the lane merges the span, the hand-resolved hunk gets a read.

<<~/ahu>>

